<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Severus Alexander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">208–235</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Alexander Severus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Severus Alexander was Roman emperor from 222 to 235, the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severan-dynasty">Severan dynasty</a>, who came to the throne as a boy under the guidance of his mother Julia Mamaea. He fought an inconclusive war against the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>, then moved to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> to meet Germanic raids. His attempt to buy peace angered the army, which killed him and his mother near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> in 235, opening the crisis of the third century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/severus-alexander.jpg" alt="Severus Alexander" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Severus_Musei_Capitolini_MC471.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
